FINDINGS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
F1 (observation, in-scope-adjacent, NOT a defect). The new equality test uses
   budgetTarget=1, healthcareTarget=1 with tolerance 0.2 so that a
   pre-existing, deliberately out-of-scope difference between the two walks'
   TARGET accrual formulas (metrics.go prorates by MonthsBetween's fractional
   day count; the chart uses a flat monthly rate — master behavior, per
   buildBudgetVsActualChartData's own comment) shrinks below the threshold
   while the SPEND-side bug stays at full scale. I verified the separation is
   real rather than tuned: under W_revert the divergence is $800.04/$800.12,
   ~4000x the tolerance, and my own independent overlap probe reproduced
   agreement at the same tolerance on a different fixture. The consequence
   worth recording is that this test cannot detect a future regression in the
   TARGET accrual, only in the SPEND accrual. That matches ruling e's scope
   exactly, but it means "the two walks agree" is guaranteed by this test
   only for the spend term.
F2 (backlog, unchanged from my attempt-3 verdict, PRE-EXISTING/master-native).
   CombinedCumulativeBalance's per-month |sum| partition assumption still
   breaks on a refund-dominant month; my attempt-3 both-ends probe showed it
   failing identically with planExclusions=nil. Attempt 4 makes the CHART
   agree with metrics.go, which is what was asked — it does not fix the
   shared underlying assumption. Still worth its own task.
F3 (commit hygiene, unchanged): untracked, non-gitignored 16MB ELF
   `budget2.old-1345` in the repo root would be swept up by `git add -A`.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
The scoped remediation does exactly what ruling SY-2026-08-30e asked and
nothing else. Scope is proven at the byte level against my own attempt-3
hashes: of the fifteen SY4.3 files, exactly one moved. The walk now merges
the two already-classified buckets and takes ONE Abs; my Hash-level probe
shows the HI+flagged overlap row appearing exactly once, a non-HI flagged row
zero times, and quantifies the old two-Abs shape's error at $2,200 on that
fixture. The required mutation fails BOTH subtests including the nil-map one
that represents the master regression. The set-exclusion control, the chart
wiring mutant and a bar-value mutant of my own all still kill, so the rewrite
disconnected neither the bar nor the wiring. 32 SY4 tests pass by name, whole
tree green, both files byte-identical after every mutation.
